    "body": "<!-- linear-linkback -->\n<details>\n<summary><a href=\"https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4673/cc5-sce5aaf-check-m2s-flow-and-reply-alerts-in-the-packaged-desktop\">TXE-4673 [CC5-sce5aaf] Check M2's Flow and reply alerts in the packaged desktop app on the real API (NC-08h)</a></summary>\n<p>\n\nDeliverable consumer: okr\n\nPart of the NC-08 split (TXE-4622) for TXE-4500. Coordinator disposition 2026-10-19 (Orca msg_11753a034972): a new scoped NC-08 native-journey layer, owned by CC5.\n\n**What it checks, in the packaged desktop app on a run-owned real stack (macOS):**\n\n* A real producer input for each Flow kind (flow_mention, flow_support_added, flow_support_done, flow_source_changed) and both reply kinds (discussion_reply, flow_discussion_reply) gives the signed-in person exactly one desktop alert, with that kind's text and the Notification Center entry route (NC-07, TXE-4499/TXE-4595 capability `notification-center/v1`).\n* An item read before its alert is due is never alerted.\n* Clicking the alert opens the entry route in the app; once the web client shows the flow and replies groups (CC1's capability follow-up), the exact destination is revealed and focused and the row is read on the server. Until then the journey records what the renderer shows and is not claimed.\n\n**Evidence rules:** alerts are captured by the shell's test notification sink (`OKR_DESKTOP_NOTIFY_LOG`); that is recorded as \"handed to the OS notifier stand-in\", never as an observed OS banner. No change to the installed app or the person's profile; run-owned test package with `OKR_DESKTOP_TEST_NO_PROTOCOL_CLIENT=1`; an isolated run manifest is published and a native lease granted before any launch. The person's profile is reported unattributable while their app runs.\n\n**Out of scope:** the `CLIENT_GROUPS` switch itself (CC1), activation (TXE-4605 #3898, held), any production write.\n</p>\n</details>\n<details>\n<summary><a href=\"https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4500/cc-codex-fcd10a7ba73d-verify-staged-notification-center-feature\">TXE-4500 [CC-codex-fcd10a7ba73d] Verify staged Notification Center feature delivery across clients</a></summary>\n<p>\n\nDeliverable consumer: okr → workstream: okr.\n\nParent: [TXE-4490](https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4490) · Plan key: **NC-08** · Execution plan: **v2** · Phase: **feature**\n\n## Outcome and scope\n\nOwn composed functional acceptance with two evidence checkpoints. Prepare the harness early under an explicit coordinator assignment. M1: after NC-01/02/04/05/06/09 merge, drive actual existing OKR producers through the complete in-app browser/shared-desktop path and record usable-release evidence. Keep this ticket In Progress; M1 is not full-scope completion.\n\nM2: after all feature integrations merge, verify every functional acceptance criterion and all five real journeys, including Flow, participant replies, upgraded native routing and installed desktop. Include accessibility, exact target/history, identity/revocation and concurrency evidence at actual source/harness revisions. This ticket supplies no formal performance pass or security audit: NC-AC26 belongs to NC-10 afterward, NC-AC31 to NC-11 afterward. Record source-group activation/release prerequisites and distinguish deployment readiness from an actual authorized rollout.\n\n## Scheduling and ownership\n\nPreferred profile: **CC5**, within Connor's selected **CC1, CC3, CC4 and CC5** pool. This is prospective, not an active holder assignment. Preserve each profile's configured model/effort and installed bypass-permissions policy. The coordinator may reassign unstarted work by readiness; one implementation owner owns each PR through its review and merge.\n\nUse [Execution Plan v2](<obsidian://open?vault=TXE&file=Project%20Magi%2FOKR%2FNotification%20Center%2FExecution%20Plan>) and Task Map.json for distinct preparation/interface/merge gates. Work can be prepared against acknowledged pinned contracts; fixture readiness is not a real merge or activation. Refill lanes continuously, with at most one approved successor and two unmerged PRs per worker.\n\n## Acceptance owned by this slice\n\nThese criteria apply at the layer named above; all other owners remain recorded in the acceptance matrix. Full functional integration is NC-08; performance is NC-10 afterward; additional security review is NC-11 afterward.\n\n* **NC-AC23** — All controls are keyboard accessible; Escape/focus return work; unread status is not conveyed only by color; screen-reader announcements are batched; reduced motion and both themes remain legible. Verification: Component/browser checks plus actual screen-reader and reduced-motion observations.\n* **NC-AC28** — Activation requires all source-writing API/worker versions and the complete UI contracts; disabling the UI preserves production of inbox records. Migration/rollback prerequisites and native compatibility are documented. Verification: Code/config inventory and release-readiness record; no deployment is implied by this acceptance ticket.\n* **NC-AC29** — Real source actions traverse producer → persisted inbox → live browser/installed desktop → exact destination → server-confirmed read state, including cross-session synchronization. Verification: Composed two-person browser and installed-desktop recordings/screenshots plus API/state evidence at the tested revision.\n* **NC-AC32** — The shared contracts/primitives are delivered by NC-09; this ticket proves only its own consumer or composed layer. NC-05/NC-06 integrate the real API independently, and NC-08 verifies the composed activation path. NC-09 closes on its library/contract tests without waiting for downstream merges.\n\n## Merge prerequisites\n\n* [TXE-4496](https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4496/cc-codex-fcd10a7ba73d-show-the-latest-unread-notification-in-the) — Show the latest unread notification in the header and dropdown\n* [TXE-4497](https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4497/cc-codex-fcd10a7ba73d-add-the-full-notifications-page-and-history) — Add the full Notifications page and history navigation\n* [TXE-4499](https://linear.app/capso/issue/TXE-4499/cc-codex-fcd10a7ba73d-connect-native-alerts-to-exact-inbox) — Complete Flow destinations and native notification routing\n\nPreparation/interface gates are separate. The complete source-group and composed-evidence activation requirements remain in the execution plan. M1 is the approved useful existing-OKR release; M2 completes Flow/replies/upgraded native routes; M3 performance; M4 security.\n\n## Source of record\n\n[Acceptance](<obsidian://open?vault=TXE&file=Project%20Magi%2FOKR%2FNotification%20Center%2FAcceptance>) · [Execution Plan](<obsidian://open?vault=TXE&file=Project%20Magi%2FOKR%2FNotification%20Center%2FExecution%20Plan>) · [System Design](<obsidian://open?vault=TXE&file=Project%20Magi%2FOKR%2FNotification%20Center%2FSystem%20Design>)\n\n[Locked decisions](<obsidian://open?vault=TXE&file=Project%20Magi%2FOKR%2FNotification%20Center%2FDecisions>) · [Ticket map](<obsidian://open?vault=TXE&file=Project%20Magi%2FOKR%2FNotification%20Center%2FTickets>) · [Acceptance](<obsidian://open?vault=TXE&file=Project%20Magi%2FOKR%2FNotification%20Center%2FAcceptance>) · [Orchestrator handoff](<obsidian://open?vault=TXE&file=Project%20Magi%2FOKR%2FNotification%20Center%2FHandoff>)\n\nRun the slice's focused tests and current repository build/test/review requirements. Record actual producer/runtime observations where the contract requires them, and realistic failing evidence for new rejection/inventory guards. Review uses review-fix v2 and merge uses the repository's own script. One ticket corresponds to one merge; obey the contract if work needs further splitting.\n\nImplementation has not started at this planning revision. No assignee, Instance label, estimate or due date is invented. Deployment/release actions need the receiving run's actual authorization; source preparation for the next feature slice continues while an external rollout decision is pending.\n\n## User acceptance amendment — NC-E05 (2026-10-16)\n\nConnor explicitly removed VoiceOver-specific speech/caption/manual-observer testing and real-screen-reader observation from this run’s M1/M2 acceptance. This is descoped, not passed. No corresponding tickets are cancelled. Keyboard access, semantic labels and batched live regions, focus, contrast, zoom, reduced motion, and browser/desktop functional acceptance remain required. NC-08 remains open until its remaining full-feature scope is verified. Historical incomplete VoiceOver evidence remains recorded; no further VoiceOver interaction or host investigation is scheduled. Canonical record: Notification Center/Decisions.md NC-E05 and Acceptance.md.\n</p>\n</details>\n<!-- linear-review-link -->\n<p><a href=\"https://linear.app/capso/review/testokr-txe-4673-m2s-flow-and-reply-alerts-in-the-packaged-desktop-app-cfb06a8aded2\">Review in Linear</a></p>\n",
